# Build context for infra/Dockerfile. User data, secrets and local tooling never enter an image.
data/
.local/
.env
**/smtp.env
# Any filled-in environment file (runtime.env, smtp.env…) wherever an operator put it: infra/production/
# is copied into the image and offered as source, so only its *.env.example templates may enter.
**/*.env
.env.*
# … and its copies: runtime.env.bak, runtime.env.2026-10-01, smtp.env.orig, .env.local in a subdirectory.
**/*.env.*
**/.env.*
# Backups and editor leftovers of any file (runtime.env~, .runtime.env.swp, nginx.conf.orig).
**/*~
**/*.bak
**/*.orig
**/*.rej
**/.*.swp
**/.*.swo
**/*.swp
# Key material and credential files.
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.crt
**/*_rsa
**/*_rsa.pub
**/*_ed25519
**/*_ed25519.pub
**/*_ecdsa
**/htpasswd
**/.htpasswd
**/.pgpass
**/.npmrc
**/.pypirc
**/.netrc
**/credentials.json
**/.secrets.*
**/*_api.txt
# Databases and their journals (a copied or restored data directory, a stray backup).
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-*
**/*.sqlite
**/*.db
# Local agent coordination notes, never part of a release.
docs/agent-work/CLAUDE_CODE_HANDOFF_*.txt
docs/agent-work/.coordinator.lock*
# The templates are re-admitted last, after every rule above that would match them.
!.env.example
!**/*.env.example
.venv/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/*.egg-info/
**/__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
testdata/
docs/screenshots/
.git/
.claude/
